# Environment files - NEVER include in the Docker image.
#
# `COPY . .` baked /app/.env.production into an image layer carrying EIGHT
# secret-shaped keys, including DB_PASSWORD and DATABASE_URL for the shared
# operations database - the highest exposure measured on this box. Readable by
# anyone who can pull the image and permanent in every historical layer.
#
# The build needs no env file: its four NEXT_PUBLIC_* values arrive as build args
# and it does not query the database (no locale route is prerendered). Runtime
# config, DB credentials included, arrives via `env_file:` at container start.
#
# This removes the credential from the IMAGE. It does not remove this site's
# direct dependency on the operations DB (BOARD 23), which is a separate matter.
.env*
!.env.example
node_modules
.next
